{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1492708-general-informations-about-maria-sandoza-and-the-el-paso-massacre","id":1492708,"title":"General informations about Maria Sandoza (and the El Paso Massacre)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-09-09T13:05:57-07:00","id":1492708,"title":"General informations about Maria Sandoza (and the El Paso Massacre)","content":"Fellow scholars, I'm searching canon informations about Maria Sandoza. As i can see from the wiki the sources are very few (also including Beckett's diary).<br /> <br /> Most of all I'm interested about the lore (if exists at all) behind the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Grand_Inquisitor\" target=\"_blank\">El Paso Massacre</a> in which she was the only survivor. In the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Sabbat_Inquisition\" target=\"_blank\">Sabbat Inquisition</a> page it's written &quot;Julian was killed by his own sire under order of the True Hand in 1970, though Julian managed to slay the traitor before he died. Julian's successor did not emerge until 1973, when Mar\u00eda Sandoza became the sect's second Grand Inquisitor.&quot;, stating the Tal'Mahe'Ra involvement. Why did Maria survived? Was she lucky? Is there a deeper explaination?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26404-submariner93","name":"Submariner93","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26404_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-09T13:14:38-07:00","id":1492709,"title":"","content":"Small world. In my game, Maria Sandoza and the Sabbat Inquisition abolished the Regent position and made the Grand Inquisitor position the top of the Sabbat. I haven't been able to find any canon stuff about her either. It worked out for the best for me since she was pretty much a blank slate. I think they just kind of forgot about her towards the end of that gameline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-10T03:37:32-07:00","id":1492749,"title":"","content":"Dunno what is going on but I am also doing a Sabbat game where Maria is going to feature pretty heavily, so any info would be very welcome.<br /> <br /> As an aside, any particularly good books on the Sabbat Inquisition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Don't follow me, I'm lost too! But if you do...</b><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11263-gimmisky","name":"Gimmisky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11263_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-13T06:09:30-07:00","id":1492971,"title":"","content":"Mmm, I don't know any resource that delve directly into the Inquisition aside Montreal by Night (its metaplot and the last chapter) and one of the chapters of Rites of Blood. I think that all the other informations are scattered along the gameline so I'm interested too should anyone suggest some references.<br /> <br /> CajunKhan and Gimmisky, have you got any headcanon about Maria you want to share? Maybe about her relationship with Lucita or Moncada, or her rise to the role of Grand Inquisitor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26404-submariner93","name":"Submariner93","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26404_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-13T14:57:54-07:00","id":1493027,"title":"","content":"In my games, she's a Feral Hearter who became Grand Inquisitor for two reasons:<br /> (1)Because she felt that infernalists and heretics would be the ultimate prey.<br /> (2)Because she felt that devoting herself to the spirituality of a Path gave her genuine inner-peace, and so she believes that the Sabbat must be protected as a safe-haven for Path followers.<br /> <br /> She's made a move to seize power because she feels that the Cathari and, to a lesser extent, the Noddists have taken over the sect to its detriment. The Cathari have become bloated and incompetent by raising their shovelheads to True Sabbat status far too quickly. The Cathari have become an absolutely massive Path of incompetent hedonists as a result.<br /> <br /> The Noddists have become obsessed with diablerie and chasing any hint of the Antedeluvians to the detriment of all else.<br /> <br /> Maria yearns for a Sabbat that has a safe, stable territory in which vampires who follow Paths can advance spiritually without fear of genocide from those vampires who follow &quot;Humanity&quot; and view all Path followers as subhuman. She's skeptical of the war against the Antedeluvians, considering it possible that Antedeluvian sightings may be simply especially powerful Methuselahs who aren't worth expending massive resources hunting.<br /> <br /> Currently she hopes to conquer Louisiana and the poorer parts of the states surrounding Louisiana, and has started by successfully conquering New Orleans.. After conquering the Deep South she plans to attempt to achieve peace with the Camarilla. If she could turn the Deep South into a small Sabbat empire at peace with the Camarilla, she would be quite content.<br /> <br /> As a result, she has moved the Sabbat Inquisition to abolish the Regent position, set themselves up as the ruling body of the Sabbat with her on top, and declared the Cathari heretical.<br /> <br /> She has not declared the Noddists heretical, partly because she doesn't want a two-front war, but also because she still has some hope that they can be restored to a balanced, spiritual path that values the survival of the Sabbat and the protection of Sabbat territory just as much as it values hunting Antedeluvians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 09-14-2022, 02:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}